   "date": "2015-12-29T02:08:03Z",
   "subject": "Data Manipulation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello DRUG users<div><br></div><div>I have a DF with two variables. </div><div><br></div><div><div>rail &lt;- c(&quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;, &quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;,&quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;)</div><div>car &lt;- c(&quot;Sometimes&quot;, &quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;,&quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;,&quot;Sometimes&quot;)</div><div>df &lt;- as.data.frame(cbind(rail, car))<br></div><div><br></div></div><div>I want to create a summary DF where the columns (variables) are (1) Mode: Two categories - rail and car, (2) Often, (3) Sometimes, (4) Rarely. The values are the counts of responses. Please see attachment. </div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"260\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:260pt\">\r\n\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"65\" span=\"4\" style=\"width:65pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" width=\"65\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:65pt\">Mode</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">Often</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">Sometimes</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">Rarely</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">Rail</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">Car</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">5</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n\r\n</tbody></table></div><div><br></div><div> Any suggestions how I should go about this? </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "773lUKyKAQAJ",
   "from": "Jaime Ashander",
   "author": "f8f554f3c8aec296",
   "date": "2015-12-29T02:21:43Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: Data Manipulation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The code below will get you most of the way there. (You can then create the Mode column from row.names):</div><div><br></div><div>data.frame(t(apply(df, 2, table)))<br></div><div><br></div><div>You could also check out the tidyr package (<a href=\"http://blog.rstudio.org/2014/07/22/introducing-tidyr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://blog.rstudio.org/2014/07/22/introducing-tidyr/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467647853000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3yL0MO64YlAyneVIiNoUld\">http://blog.rstudio.org/2014/07/22/introducing-tidyr/</a>) which provides several flexible functions to do stuff like this.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Jaime</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Dec 28, 2015 at 6:08 PM, Gouri Shankar Mishra <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gouri....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello DRUG users<div><br></div><div>I have a DF with two variables. </div><div><br></div><div><div>rail &lt;- c(&quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;, &quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;,&quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;)</div><div>car &lt;- c(&quot;Sometimes&quot;, &quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;,&quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;,&quot;Sometimes&quot;)</div><div>df &lt;- as.data.frame(cbind(rail, car))<br></div><div><br></div></div><div>I want to create a summary DF where the columns (variables) are (1) Mode: Two categories - rail and car, (2) Often, (3) Sometimes, (4) Rarely. The values are the counts of responses. Please see attachment. </div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"260\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:260pt\">\r\n\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"65\" span=\"4\" style=\"width:65pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" width=\"65\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:65pt\">Mode</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">Often</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">Sometimes</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">Rarely</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">Rail</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">Car</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">5</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n\r\n</tbody></table></div><div><br></div><div> Any suggestions how I should go about this? </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nCheck out our R resources at <a href=\"http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467647853000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1JysL2bkMIEubfx9kXhQdi\">http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Davis R Users&#39; Group&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">davis-rug+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467647853000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1p4wfcb5AckcSqG_S3W1K4\">https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467647853000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1w-rI4cxe7WouhEA9bWwJm\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
