  {
   "id": "wOvzmNGKAQAJ",
   "from": "Michael Koontz",
   "author": "47ca46208a81ec5e",
   "date": "2015-12-29T02:24:23Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: Data Manipulation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">+1 to Jaime’s answer.<div><br></div><div>Here’s one way to reformat the result to look like what is in the Excel spreadsheet.</div><div><br></div><div><div>foo &lt;- apply(df, MARGIN=2, FUN=table)</div><div>foo</div><div><br></div><div># Use the t() function to transpose our matrix-like object</div><div>transposed_foo &lt;- t(foo)</div><div><br></div><div># Coerce our object to a data.frame</div><div>df_foo &lt;- data.frame(transposed_foo)</div><div><br></div><div># Make a new column called &#39;Mode&#39; that uses the rownames of the object created with table()</div><div>df_foo$Mode &lt;- rownames(df_foo)</div><div><br></div><div># Reorder the columns in the object</div><div>d &lt;- df_foo[, c(4, 1, 3, 2)]</div><div><br></div><div># Overwrite the leftover rownames from the original table() call</div><div>rownames(d) &lt;- 1:nrow(d)</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;word-wrap:break-word\"><div><br>--</div><div>Michael Koontz — <a href=\"http://michaeljkoontz.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://michaeljkoontz.weebly.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467647858000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0sL5cTMCjH-y5suK6pnogW\">website</a></div><div>Graduate Group in Ecology</div><div><a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Plant+and+Environmental+Sciences+Bldg,+University+of+California,+Davis,+Davis,+CA+95616/@38.5427751,-121.7570251,16z/data=!4m2!3m1!1s0x808529085c693a13:0xe20b0046ee4eb4f7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.google.com/maps/place/Plant%2Band%2BEnvironmental%2BSciences%2BBldg,%2BUniversity%2Bof%2BCalifornia,%2BDavis,%2BDavis,%2BCA%2B95616/@38.5427751,-121.7570251,16z/data%3D!4m2!3m1!1s0x808529085c693a13:0xe20b0046ee4eb4f7&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467647858000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3aITM9W1rYBcK85dSp_wdT\">Plant and Environmental Sciences</a>, Room 2211</div><div>University of California, Davis</div><div>Davis, CA 95616</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div><br></div><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">\r\n</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>\r\n<br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Dec 28, 2015, at 6:21 PM, Jaime Ashander &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jash...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The code below will get you most of the way there. (You can then create the Mode column from row.names):</div><div><br></div><div>data.frame(t(apply(df, 2, table)))<br></div><div><br></div><div>You could also check out the tidyr package (<a href=\"http://blog.rstudio.org/2014/07/22/introducing-tidyr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://blog.rstudio.org/2014/07/22/introducing-tidyr/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467647858000&amp;usg=AOvVaw12wAPx5q1bjmf5AkGuNyWD\">http://blog.rstudio.org/2014/07/22/introducing-tidyr/</a>) which provides several flexible functions to do stuff like this.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Jaime</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Dec 28, 2015 at 6:08 PM, Gouri Shankar Mishra <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gouri....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello DRUG users<div><br></div><div>I have a DF with two variables. </div><div><br></div><div><div>rail &lt;- c(&quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;, &quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;,&quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;)</div><div>car &lt;- c(&quot;Sometimes&quot;, &quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;,&quot;Often&quot;, &quot;Rarely&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;, &quot;Sometimes&quot;,&quot;Sometimes&quot;)</div><div>df &lt;- as.data.frame(cbind(rail, car))<br></div><div><br></div></div><div>I want to create a summary DF where the columns (variables) are (1) Mode: Two categories - rail and car, (2) Often, (3) Sometimes, (4) Rarely. The values are the counts of responses. Please see attachment. </div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"260\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:260pt\">\r\n\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"65\" span=\"4\" style=\"width:65pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" width=\"65\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:65pt\">Mode</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">Often</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">Sometimes</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">Rarely</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">Rail</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">Car</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">5</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n\r\n</tbody></table></div><div><br></div><div> Any suggestions how I should go about this? </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nCheck out our R resources at <a href=\"http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467647858000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1EXDGQKSY_Ns5d_d7OFvJZ\">http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Davis R Users&#39; Group&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">davis-rug+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>